--  Source of truth for the names: the extraction's own
--  _migration/meta/columns.csv. 191 columns, most of them Arabic;
--  retyping them is where a silent error would enter.
--
--  EVERY SOURCE COLUMN IS `text`, nullable, with no default and no
--  check. A load must not be able to fail on a bad date or a
--  non-numeric number — those arrive intact and are dealt with at
--  Gate 3, where the firm can see them. A row rejected at the door
--  is a row nobody ever sees again.
--
--  NULL and empty string stay distinct. An unassigned `lawyerA` is
--  not the same as one that was cleared. The extractor writes NULL
--  as a bare empty field and '' as "", and PostgreSQL CSV COPY reads
--  back exactly that distinction, so the schema only has to stay out
--  of the way.
--
--  Names are VERBATIM — Arabic, `Cash/probono`, `Inv-No` and all.
--  Staging must be directly comparable to the source. Renaming to
--  snake_case ASCII happens at transform, stage D.
